WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.490
A government pays builders 100
million to put up a new bridge.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.120
The bridge opens, the
builders have been paid,

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.730
and the job is finished.

4
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.350
Yet when the country's income is added up,

5
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.450
it can have grown by more
than that 100 million.

6
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.320
So if a government spends 1 billion,

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.410
why can the country's
income grow by much more?

8
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.930
In this mission, you'll follow
that spending round by round,

9
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.520
and add up the total.

10
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.030
Then you'll move one
slider in a graph lab,

11
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.980
predict what happens to the total,

12
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.180
and test it.

13
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.500
Your mission: find out how
one injection of spending

14
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.680
grows into far more income.
